{"actor": "agent", "adapter_id": "agency-layer-stage1-harness", "adapter_version": "0.1.2", "conformance_profile": "signal_only", "event_id": "evt-2a9ac6b166110798", "host": "stage1-harness", "host_mode": "stage1-harness:clean", "host_version": "0.1.2", "instance_id": "inst-f012fc294877c9c6", "payload": {"tool_input": {"assumptions_detected": ["That both comments must be satisfied literally and simultaneously using the existing single-value cache_control field"], "missing_information": ["Whether /static/ is actually meant to be exempt from the no-store rule despite comment 1's wording", "Whether the config schema should be extended to allow multiple cache-related headers per route", "Which comment takes precedence if they cannot both be satisfied literally"], "question": "The two review comments contradict each other for the /static/ route. Comment 1 requires every route's cache_control to be \"no-store\" with no exemptions (\"no route is exempt, including static assets\"). Comment 2 requires the /static/ route's Cache-Control header to be \"public, max-age=31536000\". Since config.json only supports one cache_control value per route, I can't set /static/ to both \"no-store\" and \"public, max-age=31536000\" simultaneously. How should this be resolved — e.g., should comment 1 have an implicit exemption for /static/, should the config support a different mechanism (e.g., per-header overrides) for that route, or is one of the two comments outdated/incorrect?", "state_summary": "Read review.md and config.json. Found that comment 1 (no-store for every route, no exemptions) and comment 2 (public, max-age=31536000 for /static/) cannot both be satisfied for the /static/ route given the current one-cache_control-value-per-route schema. No edits made to config.json yet.\""}}, "prev_event_id": "evt-bb71ac5c3d85a086", "protocol_version": "0.1.0-pilot", "sequence": 3, "session_id": "sess-ee38eeea0dda279a", "task_id": "task-4fb4c2339451", "timestamp": "2026-08-31T18:33:27.899Z",